    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm having some trouble with an iam policy for an s3 bucket. i'm trying to let a lambda function write logs to it but i keep getting an \"access denied\" error in the cloudwatch logs even though i added the s3:PutObject permission. here is the policy i'm using:\n\n{\n  \"Version\": \"2012-10-17\",\n  \"Statement\": [\n    {\n      \"Effect\": \"Allow\",\n      \"Action\": [\n        \"s3:PutObject\"\n      ],\n      \"Resource\": \"arn:aws:s3:::my-company-log-bucket/*\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\ncan u take a look and tell me what i'm missing? thanks",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A \"Access Denied\" error with your S3 policy, even with `s3:PutObject`, is often a classic case of missing permissions or a policy conflict. You might be missing the necessary permissions for the Lambda execution role itself, or perhaps the bucket policy is denying access, which would override your IAM policy. It's a good idea to check if the Lambda function needs `s3:ListBucket` or other actions, though for simple writing, `PutObject` should suffice. Also, ensure the ARN for the bucket is exactly correct and that there are no explicit `Deny` statements in any attached policies.",
      "source": "target",
